cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FinTFM: a tabular foundation model for corporate credit risk, pretrained only on synthetic data"
message: >-
  If you use this software, the checkpoint, or the measurement log, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Organokov
    given-names: Mukharbek
    email: mukharbek.organokov@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/kabartay/fintfm"
url: "https://huggingface.co/kabartay/fintfm-binary"
abstract: >-
  An in-context tabular classifier for corporate credit risk, pretrained
  exclusively on synthetic data and never on real tables. Prediction is a single
  forward pass with the user's table supplied as context; there are no gradient
  steps at fit time and no per-dataset tuning. The repository is organised around
  a numbered measurement log and a claims ledger that records retractions and
  superseded results as prominently as confirmations. Measured externally on
  TabArena it places 93rd of 95; on real corporate-default panels its calibration
  is consistently among the best measured while its discrimination consistently
  loses to tuned gradient boosting. Both facts are reported together.
keywords:
  - tabular foundation model
  - in-context learning
  - prior-fitted networks
  - credit risk
  - synthetic data
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
